            <ArticleTitle>Eye pain due to carotid stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1056-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 63-year-old woman presented with the acute onset of right eye pain. Ophthalmic and neurologic examinations were normal except for a loud right carotid bruit. Directional Doppler examination suggested a critical stenosis of the internal carotid artery. Subsequent arteriography revealed a 95% stenosis. The eye pain ceased following carotid endarterectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
